# Route conventions (`client/src/routes/`)

## Groups

- `_authenticated/` holds every page that needs a session; its `beforeLoad` starts the OIDC
  login. `_public/` holds the pages anyone opens ([ADR 0003](../../docs/adr/0003-public-and-authenticated-routes.md));
  `RootLayout` renders them in `PublicLayout`, and they only call public endpoints through
  `xhandlerPublicClient`.
- Paths are Spanish and follow the hierarchy of [ADR 0002](../../docs/adr/0002-navigation-partner-tenant-company.md):
  `/organizaciones/$tenantId/empresas/$companyId`, `/padron/…`, `/perfil`, `/p/documentos/$token`.
- `padron.ts` 404s every searchpe page when searchpe isn't deployed; a new optional product gets
  the same guard ([ADR 0001](../../docs/adr/0001-one-shell-two-backends.md)).

## Route files

- A route file only wires `createFileRoute` options (`validateSearch`, `search`, `beforeLoad`,
  `loader`, `pendingComponent`, `errorComponent`, `component`) to a page from `@app/pages/...`.
  No page JSX, hooks or queries; no `lazy()` (routes are auto code-split).
- A list route passes `validateSearch` and `search` from `listSearch(<LIST>_STATE)`
  ([list-state](list-state.md)).
- A pathless or path layout (`_authenticated.ts`, `_public.ts`, `padron.ts`,
  `organizaciones/$tenantId.ts`) has no `component`; the router renders `<Outlet />`.

## Detail routes

- The loader primes the detail query with `queryClient.query({ …options, staleTime: "static" })`
  from its params (`tenantId` included) and returns the ids the page needs.
- `pendingComponent` is `DetailRoutePending` labelled `Cargando <objeto>`, no ellipsis;
  `errorComponent` is `DetailRouteError` (a 404 and a foreign tenant look the same). The page
  uses `useSuspense*Query` and has no loading or not-found guards.
- `component` is a `*DetailRoute.tsx` adapter next to the page: it reads loader data or params
  with `getRouteApi("<exact route id>")` and passes them as props.

```tsx
// routes/_authenticated/organizaciones/$tenantId/empresas/$companyId.tsx
export const Route = createFileRoute(
  "/_authenticated/organizaciones/$tenantId/empresas/$companyId",
)({
  loader: async ({
    context: { queryClient },
    params: { tenantId, companyId },
  }) => {
    await queryClient.query({
      ...companyDetailQueryOptions({ tenantId, companyId }),
      staleTime: "static",
    });
    return { companyId };
  },
  pendingComponent: () => <DetailRoutePending label="Cargando empresa" />,
  errorComponent: DetailRouteError,
  component: CompanyDetailRoute,
});
```

## Params, search and links

- Pages and components never read path params; the one exception is `useSelectedTenantId()`.
- A page may read and update its own route's search params only through
  `getRouteApi("<its route id>").useSearch()` / `.useNavigate()`.
- `validateSearch` returns a typed fallback for each key and never throws.
- Internal links use typed `to` + `params` (`<Link>`, `navigate`), never a template-string URL.

## Checklist

Pass/fail rubric for `/eval`. Check changed files under `client/src/routes/`, `router.ts`,
`*Route.tsx`, and pages that read search params.

- [ ] Private pages are under `_authenticated/`, public ones under `_public/`; paths are Spanish
      and carry tenant/company ids.
- [ ] Route files only wire options to a page; layouts have no `component`.
- [ ] Detail loaders prime the detail query with `staleTime: "static"` and return ids.
- [ ] `DetailRoutePending` with `Cargando <objeto>` (no ellipsis) and `DetailRouteError`.
- [ ] Adapters read through `getRouteApi` with the exact route id and pass props.
- [ ] Pages read no path params (except `useSelectedTenantId`) and read search only for their
      own route via `getRouteApi`.
- [ ] `validateSearch` has typed fallbacks; internal links are typed.
